  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: SearchParameter be-sp-serviceRequest-intent-or-prescription-type</b></p><a name=\"be-sp-serviceRequest-intent-or-prescription-type\"> </a><a name=\"hcbe-sp-serviceRequest-intent-or-prescription-type\"> </a><h2>BeReferralIntentOrPrescriptionType</h2><p>Parameter <code>intent-or-prescription-type</code>:<code>token</code></p><div><p>Matches ServiceRequests whose intent OR prescriptionType category matches any of the given tokens. Qualify each value with its system: http://hl7.org/fhir/request-intent for intent, https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/terminology/CodeSystem/be-cs-prescription-type for the prescriptionType slice of category. Example: GET [base]/ServiceRequest?intent-or-prescription-type=proposal,telemonitoring-chronic-heart-failure</p>\n</div><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td>Resource</td><td><a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/servicerequest.html\">ServiceRequest</a></td></tr><tr><td>Expression</td><td><code>ServiceRequest.intent | ServiceRequest.category.where(coding.system = 'https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/terminology/CodeSystem/be-cs-prescription-type')</code></td></tr><tr><td>Multiples</td><td><ul><li>multipleAnd: The parameter may only appear once</li><li>multipleOr: The parameter may have multiple values (separated by comma) where at least one must be true</li></ul></td></tr></table></div>"
